  "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed (in miles per hour), we divide the number of miles, $12,$ by the number of hours, $20.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{20} & =\\frac{12\u00f72}{20\u00f72} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{10} \\\\  & =6\u00f710 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of starfish is $0.6$ miles per hour.",
